sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To construct an isosceles triangle having each of the angles at the base double the remaining one.
----
proof:

Set out any straight line *AB,* and cut it at the point *C* so that the rectangle *AB* by *BC* equals the square on *CA.*  Describe the circle *BDE* with center A and radius *AB.*  Fit in the circle *BDE* the straight line *BD* equal to the straight line *AC* which is not greater than the diameter of the circle *BDE.* [!just II.11; IV.1]

Join *AD* and *DC,* and circumscribe the circle *ACD* about the triangle *ACD.* [!just IV.5]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="300" height="300" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IV.10 diagram" src="propIV10.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
